### lib-dart-e2e
#### source: lib/dart/e2e
# Flutter-only generated plugin manifests. This member depends on the Flutter SDK
# (transitively, because the version train includes diene_auth_engine and
# diene_api_engine), so `flutter pub get` writes files the pure-Dart siblings
# never produce and the inherited dart-lib list therefore never covered.
#
# MEASURED, not reasoned. Real CI at 65c9777 failed Nix Flake Check while all six
# other jobs passed, and the failing hook's own output says
# "No issues found! … ✅ Dart analysis passed" immediately above
# "- files were modified by this hook". Analyze was never the problem.
#
# THE ACTUAL CAUSE WAS THAT THE FILE WAS **TRACKED**, committed by accident in
# 923157c, so every `flutter pub get` REWROTE a tracked file and pre-commit
# correctly reported a modification. Ignoring it was necessary and NOT sufficient:
# `.gitignore` has no effect on an already-tracked path, which is why the first
# attempt at this fix changed nothing and `git check-ignore` still returned 1. The
# fix is `git rm --cached` PLUS these entries; verified afterwards with the PLAIN
# check-ignore form (rc=0) and with `-v` naming this exact line, because `-v`
# alone is not a verdict — it also reports negations.
#
# That also explains why local `flutter analyze` was rc=0 while CI was red: both
# were true. Locally the tracked file's content already matched, so nothing
# appeared modified; CI checked out a fresh tree where `pub get` produced
# different bytes. Entries match the accepted api-engine and auth-engine sets
# rather than inventing a third spelling.
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
